QGC WPL 110
# ============================================================================
# AIRSPEED + LIDAR STAIRCASE SENSOR VALIDATION
# Takeoff → Straight East over 5 platforms → Right-hand racetrack → Straight West → Land
#
# Coordinate origin: lat=-35.363262, lon=149.165237 (CMAC)
# Platform centerline: lat=-35.363262 (Y=0 in world frame)
# Platform positions:  X=250/350/450/550/650m East of home
# Cruise altitude:     30m AGL
# Intended world:      worlds/mini_talon_airspeed_lidar/wind_staircase.sdf
# Intended params:     config/mini_talon_airspeed_lidar/plane_full.parm
#
# RACETRACK DESIGN — inherited from the wind-world eastbound takeoff frame:
#
#   WP7  (950E,   0N) → heading East  — overshoots P5 by 300m
#   WP8  (950E, 150S) → right 90°, heading South
#   WP9  (850E, 150S) → right 90°, heading West
#   WP10 (850E,   0N) → left 90° back to the eastbound centerline, now heading West
#   WP11 (650E,   0N) → centerline rejoin before platform 5 on the westbound leg
#
# Why the staircase starts at 250m:
#   `00000169.BIN` showed the aircraft only reached about X=90m and ~4.4m AGL on
#   the failed run, which is not enough margin to clear a 5m platform at X=100m.
#   The staircase is shifted downrange so takeoff and climb can settle first.
#
# Why 950m overshoot:
#   Gives WP7→WP8 enough room to stabilize before the southbound offset leg, while
#   keeping the aircraft aligned with the wind-world runway frame on departure.
#
# Nav params (plane_full.parm):
#   NAVL1_PERIOD=13  → L1 lookahead ≈ 58m (stable, tight tracking)
#   NAVL1_DAMPING=0.85 → prevents oscillation with tighter period
#   WP_RADIUS=10m    → exactly the platform half-width (20m/2), forces overpass
#   Gazebo wind is active in the world, SITL wind stays disabled here
# ============================================================================

